\fs28 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
##Early Origins: Narrow Skirt Era (1908\'961914)
\fs24 \
\
\
Where: France, United States\
\uc0\u8232 Fashion context: The introduction of the 
\f1\i hobble skirt
\f0\i0  marked the first widespread appearance of narrower, straight skirts.\
\uc0\u8232 Key figures: Paul Poiret (often associated with early narrow silhouettes\'96 la robe entrav\'e9e).\
\uc0\u8232 Characteristics:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Very narrow hems that limited movement, especially walking\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Long, columnlike silhouette\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Decorative banding or draping that stressed verticality. Most importantly, accentuated hips that highlighted \'93feminine\'94 features.\uc0\u8232 Fabric: Wool, silk, satin blends typical of Edwardian fashion.\u8232 Shift: Introduced the idea of restriction + elegance through narrowness\'97a predecessor to the pencil skirt.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\

\fs28 ##Interwar Period\'a0(1918-1939)\
\

\fs24 \
Where: Europe and North America\
\uc0\u8232 Fashion context: Hemlines rose and skirts overall became slimmer\'96 changing the hobble skirt\'92s appearance to a more \'93modern\'94 one.\
\uc0\u8232 Characteristics:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Straight, tubular skirts (often mid-calf)\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
More freedom of movement than the hobble skirt\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Early versions of side or back slits\uc0\u8232 Fabric: Lightweight wool, rayon, silk crepe.\u8232 Shift: Transition from ornamental Edwardian shapes to functional style\'97a premature foundation for the pencil skirt.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\

\fs28 ##Wartime (1940\'961945)\
\

\fs24 \
Where: US, UK, France\
\uc0\u8232 Historical influence: WWII fabric rationing enforced narrower skirts and shorter hems.\
\uc0\u8232 Characteristics:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Functional knee-length straight skirts\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Less fabric, simple seams, limited decoration\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Early \'93utility\'94 tailoring that emphasized economy\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
We see a skirt that will eventually shape the style of the pencil skirt, but the skirt itself has not been invented yet.\uc0\u8232 Fabric: Wool blends, rayon, gabardine.\u8232 Shift: Practicality + rationing normalized the slim skirt\'97and prepared the silhouette that Dior would later formalize.\
\pard\tx566\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 ##The Birth of the Modern Pencil Skirt (1947\'961954)
\fs24 \
Key figure: Christian Dior, Charles James\
\uc0\u8232 Where: Paris\
\uc0\u8232 Fashion context: Dior\'92s ligne H (1954) brought forth the modern pencil skirt. Charles James is not usually attributed to creating the pencil skirt, but he introduced several skirts that became a testament to the pencil skirt in 1952. Simultaneously, both Monsieur James and Monsieur Dior gave birth to the modern pencil skirt.\
\uc0\u8232 Characteristics:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Narrow, straight cut tapering toward the hem\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Structured waist emphasizing an hourglass line\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Hem typically just below the knee\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Back vent introduced for ease of walking\uc0\u8232 Fabric: Wool crepe, gabardine, heavier silks, structured synthetics emerging in the 1950s.\u8232 Shift: From wartime simplicity to sculpted femininity. This marked the 
\f1\i formal
\f0\i0  creation of what we now call the pencil skirt.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\

\fs28 ##Mid-Century Professionalism & Cin\'e9ma (1950s\'961960s)\
\

\fs24 \
Where: US and Europe\
\uc0\u8232 Fashion context: Adoption of the pencil skirt in office wear, secretarial style, and Hollywood fashion.\
\uc0\u8232 Cultural figures: Marilyn Monroe, Audrey Hepburn, businesswear icons.\
\uc0\u8232 Characteristics:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Made out of wool\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Tight, curve-defining silhouettes\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Mostly knee-length\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Beacon of femininity of the 50s immortalized by Audrey Hepburn, and Grace Kelly\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Paired with fitted blouses and jackets, usually made out of wool\uc0\u8232 Fabric: Wool suiting, tweeds\u8232 Shift: Pencil skirt becomes a symbol of sophistication, femininity (more empowered), and postwar mobility.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\

\fs28 ##Contemporary Pencil Skirt (1990s\'96Present)\
\

\fs24 \
Where: Global\
\uc0\u8232 Fashion context: Minimalism (1990s), stretch fabrics (2000s), and modern gender-neutral tailoring (2010s\'962020s).\
\uc0\u8232 Characteristics:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Stretch pencil skirts for mobility\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Midi lengths, knit pencil skirts, high-elastic fabrics\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Seen in runways, workwear, and street fashion\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Fabric: Lycra blends, jersey knit, ponte, tech fabrics, vegan leather.\
\pard\tx566\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

